From 112bcd524ae9f169faacc0c27ea8e390d666ac0c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ggbdpq <ggbdpq@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 02:14:04 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] gui tests: header-centre doesn't count WebKit's
 ResizeObserver loop notice as a page error (#3479)

webkit "en at 125%" failed 2 of 2 solo runs on main (7b1faf99), errors ==
['ResizeObserver loop completed with undelivered notifications.'], while
every layout assertion stayed green. Traced with every ResizeObserver
delivery logged per frame: sweeping the window's width in 10-point
steps, a stop between fitTop's steps has the classes it tries (tight,
cramped, inrow, crowded, packed) re-laying the header out in the same
frame, so the header's observers (.top, .brand, .actions) are told once
more, and at that stop the round lands past the loop's depth. WebKit
reports it as a page error, Chromium doesn't. The round is delivered on
the next frame and the layout settles: with every stop's geometry
snapshotted per frame, en at 125% ran 182 frames at the narrowest stop
with the header 448x46 and every class and width stable, and the sweep's
own assertions hold at every stop, Chromium and WebKit alike. That is
the same class 75aa03e1a already ruled on for purpose-filter;
group-template, group-share, group-duplicate, update-release-page and
view-scrollbar-drag take the same exemption.

The test now ignores that one message, with the reason beside it; every
layout assertion is untouched.

webkit 2 of 2 solo runs pass after, chromium is green, and taking the
exemption back out turns webkit red again. header-zoom-fit and
header-relang, the other two specs that sweep fitTop's layout and assert
no page errors, pass on both engines and are left alone.

Generated-by: GLM-5.3-Flash (ZCode)
---
 internal/gui/tests/header-centre.test.cjs | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/internal/gui/tests/header-centre.test.cjs b/internal/gui/tests/header-centre.test.cjs
index cf6dba07..73696db0 100644
--- a/internal/gui/tests/header-centre.test.cjs
+++ b/internal/gui/tests/header-centre.test.cjs
@@ -63,7 +63,13 @@ for (const engine of (process.env.BROWSER ? [process.env.BROWSER] : ["chromium",
         const ctx = await browser.newContext({ viewport: { width: Math.round(1100 / zoom), height: 600 }, deviceScaleFactor: zoom });
         await ctx.addInitScript(() => { Object.defineProperty(Navigator.prototype, "platform", { get: () => "Win32" }); });
         const page = await ctx.newPage();
-        page.on("pageerror", (e) => errors.push(e.message));
+        // WebKit reports a ResizeObserver round left to the next frame as a page
+        // error; Chromium doesn't. Sweeping the window's width, a stop between
+        // fitTop's steps has the classes it tries re-laying the header out in
+        // the same frame, so the header's observers are told once more, past
+        // the loop's depth. The round is delivered on the next frame and the
+        // layout settles; nothing is painted wrong.
+        page.on("pageerror", (e) => { if (!/^ResizeObserver loop completed with undelivered notifications/.test(e.message)) errors.push(e.message); });
         await page.route("**/*", server(lang));
         await page.goto("http://magpie.test/");
         await page.waitForSelector("#nav button.on");
